{
  "document": "TEST ENGINEER SCRATCH NOTES - 04 APR 2026\n\n09:02 - Initial both tank displays ~0.05 m, all three output lamps off.\n09:03 - Start event at 20 s looks good. T1 fill is slow/linear.\n09:06 - V1 drops out at the high target. Observed target is 0.80, not the 0.78 number in Jin's old model.\n09:07 - Stop at 220 kills all valve lamps. Tank levels hold steady through pause.\n09:08 - Start at 280 picks transfer back up; it does NOT go back to fill.\n09:11 - After T1 low there is a noticeably longer dead time than the first wait. Controls says 12 s.\n09:15 - T2 drains, then new fill comes back fairly quickly (~8 s after low).\n09:16 - Stop at 650 interrupts second fill.\n09:17 - Shut at 700: transfer + drain lamps are on together. This is intentional for SHUT, not an interlock failure.\n09:18 - Shutdown finishes quickly because there was not much inventory left after the 650 stop. System stays idle to 900 s.\n\nTerminology reminders from the screen:\n  tank1 = TK-101, tank2 = TK-102\n  valve1 = XV-101, valve2 = XV-102, valve3 = XV-103\n  'shut' is controlled drain; E-stop is outside this demo scope.\n",
